In my case it was because of this block in `opencode.json`. When this is enabled, only one instance of opencode can be launched. The second one will hang. `--print-log` shows nothing.
```json
{
  // "server": {
  //   "port": 4096,
  //   "hostname": "100.64.142.97",
  //   "mdns": false
  // },
  "autoupdate": false
}
```

@gdl-reif got a fix for that, you would need to move None openAI models off the `azure` provider, and login to the azure cognition services using `opencode auth login` and make use of this config

```json
    "azure-cognitive-services": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible", 
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://{resource_name}.openai.azure.com/openai/v1",
        "useCompletionUrls": true
      },
      "models": {
        "kimi-k2.5": {
          "id": "Kimi-K2.5",
          "limit": { "output": 10000, "context": 262144 }
        }
      }
    }
```
